# Runtime safety

- Cursor and Hermes use separate model/provider configuration.
- Hermes must remain optional and offline-safe.
- Fleet, A2A, legacy bridges, port proxies, timers, and installers are disabled.
- Initial integrations use separate stdio MCP entrypoints.
- Hermes operator profiles expose read-only tools and bounded task submission
  only. Approval response and worker tools are never operator tools.
- Listeners, when introduced later, bind to loopback and authenticate.
- Never use Hermes `--oneshot`, `--yolo`, or `--accept-hooks` for Harness work.
